earch results link to the official challenge pages, but the actual content pages (like the 2023 and 2024 results pages) returned only brief descriptions without the detailed results or problem category information. To find the specific information about OR-Tools' performance in particular problem categories, you would need to visit the actual challenge results pages directly:\n\n- 2023 Results: https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2023/results/\n- 2024 Results: https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/results/\n\nThese pages should contain detailed breakdowns of solver performance across different problem categories.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8eea84bd-ca42-4634-8e89-7c5e503d29a5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:15.712Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d26be1d6-e5fa-48e0-a9ba-2ae9366c8c61","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e58c09ae-a087-4715-93cc-babf37ff907f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SkXUHTSEobcpqT3cVr1Kdo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT UNSAT proof difficult problems Laurent Perron github issue advice\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy ortools interface (cpmpy.solvers.ortools) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/ufunc/api/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"lperron (Laurent Perron) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lperron\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"python cp-sat unsat assumption bug, is sat · Issue #2649 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/2649\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"[Scheduling seminar] Laurent Perron (Google France) | The CP-SAT solver - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vvUxusrUcpU\"},{\"title\":\"Cut generators in CPModelProto · Issue #912 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/912\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/pid/73/4963.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver not finding solution · Issue #3643 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3643\"}]\n\nThe search results show information about CP-SAT solver in general, UNSAT core extraction, and some GitHub issues, but I didn't find a specific GitHub issue that directly discusses Laurent Perron's advice on UNSAT proof difficult problems. Let me provide what I found:\n\nThe search results reveal relevant information about CP-SAT and UNSAT problems:\n\n**Key findings:**\n\n1. CP-SAT has state of the art results with parallelism on hard unsat problems.\n\n2. A \"core\" strategy from the SAT-community extracts unsatisfiable cores of the formula, which is particularly useful for model debugging.\n\n3. Fine-tuning such a solver is not a simple task, and often you do more harm than good by tinkering around.\n\n4. However, decreasing the number of search workers can actually improve the runtime for some problems, and selecting the right subsolvers that are best fitted for your problem can be worth a shot.\n\nThe search results include references to GitHub issues (like #2649 and #3643) related to CP-SAT UNSAT problems, but I couldn't locate a specific GitHub issue with detailed advice from Laurent Perron on UNSAT proof difficult problems. You may want to search directly on the OR-Tools GitHub repository (https://github.com/google/or-tools) for issues where Laurent Perron has commented on UNSAT-related challenges.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7dab961b-cd17-4c80-b516-2db0959f5123","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:16.980Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e58c09ae-a087-4715-93cc-babf37ff907f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"06da2a54-1e57-4861-b01d-1b3446e153fc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015CxeG6PUmpP6SxQ5H9rG3V","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT industrial case study large scale facility placement hours runtime\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Google vs IBM: A Constraint Solving Challenge on the Job- ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1909.08247\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Industrial-size job shop scheduling with constraint programming - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2214716022000215\"},{\"title\":\"Implementing effective operations research solutions in OR-Tools - Superlinear\",\"url\":\"https://superlinear.eu/insights/articles/implementing-effective-operations-research-solutions-in-or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"How does the CP-SAT solver works? · Issue #1508 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1508\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Optimization | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver vs. CP solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Pa5eQUoLnow\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools CP-SAT industrial case studies involving large-scale optimization problems:\n\n## Industrial Case Study: Large-Scale Job Shop Scheduling\n\nA comprehensive study compared OR-Tools (Google's open-source solver) and CP Optimizer (IBM's proprietary solver) on industrial-size job shop scheduling, using novel benchmarks comprising up to one million operations to be scheduled on up to one thousand machines to reflect real-world industrial scenarios with heavy workloads like found in the semi-conductor domain.\n\nThe comparison evaluated the completion time achieved and the time required to solve the problem instances on single-core and quad-core configurations.\n\n## Runtime Considerations\n\nWhile the search results don't explicitly state specific runtime hours for the facility placement problems, one study notes that hours were allocated to complete the search, with the aim to simulate an industrial scenario where the calculation of the schedule for the day is typically done overnight.\n\nThe research demonstrates that developments during the last decade have improved the performance of state-of-the-art constraint solvers dramatically, to the point that they can be applied also on large-scale instances.\n\nIf you need more specific runtime data or details about particular facility placement benchmarks, you may want to consult the academic papers directly, particularly the ScienceDirect article on \"Industrial-size job shop scheduling with constraint programming\" (from 2022) or the arxiv paper comparing Google vs IBM solvers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5eda23bf-d9be-40ab-bb42-721943bf46dd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:17.124Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"06da2a54-1e57-4861-b01d-1b3446e153fc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
