{"parentUuid":"2e5d5c87-96ce-476b-b297-130bc96dfdf4","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JVkBuzBjo6f1W6d9sEFfYm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pv6fvNZCYWtbh85fp6PevM","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3643","prompt":"What is the problem described? What advice did Laurent Perron give? Quote key recommendations about CP-SAT solving difficult problems, hints, num_workers, infeasibility."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2141,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2638,"cache_read_input_tokens":21066,"output_tokens":685,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2638},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2141,"output_tokens":685,"cache_read_input_tokens":21066,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2638,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoqo9J8p2pM4PFKP56nm","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b80502d3-8112-491a-8c54-43601b7eac39","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:27.265Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5a69bd7d-c914-4f02-94fd-0a74b3f6b6fc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015GHPvuSx5Tz9ZPkJPCZ6T4","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Infeasibility Subsolvers - Key Advice\n\n## Laurent Perron's Recommendations\n\nFor proving infeasibility in CP-SAT, Perron suggested focusing on specific subsolvers:\n\n**Primary subsolvers for infeasibility:**\n- \"Core, max_lp, probing*, lb_tree_search, *costs, maybe a no_lp too.\"\n\n**Important syntax note:** Perron clarified that wildcards must be expanded to actual subsolver names rather than passed literally. He referenced the source code at `cp_model_search.cc#L619` for the complete list of available subsolvers.\n\n## Context from the Discussion\n\nStuart Rogers' strategy involved:\n- Adding bounds (L ≤ z ≤ U-1) to constrain the objective function\n- Using CP-SAT to demonstrate infeasibility, thereby proving optimality of solution U\n\n**Verification suggestion:** Ryan Henszey recommended first solving the LP relaxation with PDLP to confirm basic feasibility before attempting the integer problem with tightened bounds.\n\n## Key Technical Point\n\nThe expanded subsolvers Rogers eventually specified included `probing`, `probing_max_lp`, `reduced_costs`, and `pseudo_costs`, though the solver output showed it was still using its default subsolver configuration rather than the specified parameters."}]},"uuid":"01c85524-7aee-460c-8ed5-517eabe553ae","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:28.405Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5a69bd7d-c914-4f02-94fd-0a74b3f6b6fc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2e5d5c87-96ce-476b-b297-130bc96dfdf4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0186h3NgsmaDS8otUZMztXyu","type":"tool_result","content":"# OR-Tools CP-SAT Performance in MiniZinc Challenge 2024\n\nBased on the results summary table provided, OR-Tools CP-SAT won gold in **all four main categories**: Fixed, Free, Parallel, and Open. The document does not identify specific problems where this solver lost to competitors or provide detailed problem-by-problem breakdowns.\n\nThe page indicates that \"detailed results\" can be generated through an interactive tool where users select solvers and benchmarks, but the actual detailed competition data isn't displayed in the static content shown. The challenge included 21 distinct problems ranging from real-world optimization (aircraft-disassembly, train-scheduling) to puzzles (peaceable-queens, fox-geese-corn), but specific winner information per problem isn't listed in this excerpt.\n\nTo determine which particular problems proved most challenging and their respective winners, you would need to use the \"Compute Results\" interactive feature on the actual MiniZinc Challenge website or download the detailed scoring files referenced in the page."}]},"uuid":"4a2a3d44-9909-43a8-b947-a30000c9d566","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:31.713Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2e5d5c87-96ce-476b-b297-130bc96dfdf4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b80502d3-8112-491a-8c54-43601b7eac39","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pv6fvNZCYWtbh85fp6PevM","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Solver Issue Summary\n\n## Problem Described\nThe user reported that the CP-SAT solver in OR-Tools v9.5 returns INFEASIBLE for a constraint satisfaction model that actually has valid solutions. The issue demonstrates that when specific boolean constraints are added (commented as \"add solution\"), the solver successfully finds a solution, suggesting the solver may be prematurely concluding infeasibility.\n\n## Laurent Perron's Advice\nBased on the content provided, **no specific recommendations from Laurent Perron are visible in the excerpt shown**. While Perron is listed as the assignee for this GitHub issue #3643, his actual response or guidance on solving this problem is not included in the webpage content provided.\n\nTo see his recommendations regarding:\n- Handling difficult CP-SAT problems\n- Configuration hints\n- Worker settings (num_workers)\n- Infeasibility diagnosis strategies\n\nYou would need to access the full issue thread or comments section on the GitHub repository, which are not captured in the content shared above."}]},"uuid":"cec94dba-107e-45dd-ad28-dd8e4536299e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:32.209Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b80502d3-8112-491a-8c54-43601b7eac39","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0f7d52f7-e283-4901-a50e-a4d2bf621d71","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C46mFGd16ZgkzLmszT2CMZ","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Technical Content: Long-Running Solves & Advanced Strategies\n\n## Time Limits & Status Checking\n\nFor extended solves, establish realistic time budgets. The guidance suggests: \"I typically start with a time limit between 60 and 300 seconds\" during development, though production deployments vary. Always check solver status afterward:\n\n```python\nsolver.parameters.max_time_in_seconds = 60\nstatus = solver.solve(model)\nif status == cp_model.OPTIMAL or status == cp_model.FEASIBLE:\n    # proceed with solution\n```\n\nThe five possible status codes are: `OPTIMAL`, `FEASIBLE`, `INFEASIBLE`, `MODEL_INVALID`, and `UNKNOWN`.\n\n## Proving Infeasibility & Unsatisfiable Cores\n\nFor infeasible models, CP-SAT can extract minimal unsatisfiable cores by combining assumptions with conditional constraints:\n\n```python\nindicator = model.new_bool_var('constraint_name')\nmodel.add(constraint).only_enforce_if(indicator)\nmodel.add_assumptions([indicator])\nstatus = solver.solve(model)\n# Returns indices of conflicting assumptions\nfor var_idx in solver.sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility():\n    print(model.proto.variables[var_idx].name)\n```\n\nThis isolates problematic constraint interactions automatically.\n\n## Portfolio & Worker Tuning\n\nCP-SAT uses a portfolio approach rather than search-space partitioning. Default behavior leverages all cores, but manual tuning often improves performance:\n\n```python\nsolver.parameters.num_workers = 8  # match physical cores, not hyperthreads\n```\n\nThe document notes that \"reducing the number of workers can actually improve runtime\" by allowing remaining workers higher frequency and better memory bandwidth. Worker counts determine which subsolvers activate:\n\n- **1 worker**: default_lp only\n- **2+ workers**: heuristics (LNS variants) enabled\n- **5+ workers**: first-solution subsolvers added\n- **32+ workers**: all 15 full-problem subsolvers active\n\n## Subsolver Management\n\nInspect log blocks for performance attribution:\n\n```\nSolutions (7)             Num   Rank\n            'no_lp':    3  [1,7]\n    'quick_restart':    1  [3,3]\n```\n\nNumbers indicate count and rank ranges. Strategies absent from logs underperform for your problem. Add custom subsolvers without disrupting portfolio balance:\n\n```python\nfrom ortools.sat import sat_parameters_pb2\n\ncustom = sat_parameters_pb2.SatParameters()\ncustom.name = \"MyPackingSubsolver\"\ncustom.use_area_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d = True\nsolver.parameters.subsolver_params.append(custom)\nsolver.parameters.extra_subsolvers.append(custom.name)\n```\n\nOnly one worker slows if parameters harm performance; others continue unaffected.\n\n## Hints & Warm-Starting\n\nProvide solution guidance to accelerate convergence:\n\n```python\nmodel.add_hint(x, 1)\nmodel.add_hint(y, 2)\n```\n\nVerify feasibility before deployment:\n\n```python\nsolver.parameters.fix_variables_to_their_hinted_value = True\nstatus = solver.solve(model)\nif status == cp_model.INFEASIBLE:\n    print(\"Hints conflict with constraints\")\n```\n\nComplete partial hints automatically via constraint propagation with the `complete_hint()` helper provided in the documentation.\n\n## Large Neighborhood Search (LNS)\n\nDisable full problem solving to run heuristics only:\n\n```python\nsolver.parameters.use_lns_only = True\n# Must pair with max_time_in_seconds; incomplete subsolvers lack stopping criteria\n```\n\n## Presolve & Complexity Management\n\nLong-running models may suffer from excessive presolve overhead. The primer cautions: \"if your model is relatively simple…you might consider reducing the presolve effort.\"\n\n```python\nsolver.parameters.max_presolve_iterations = 3\nsolver.parameters.cp_model_probing_level = 1\nsolver.parameters.presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit = 5\n```\n\nReview logs to identify which presolve techniques consume time before adjusting.\n\n## Case Study: Model Building Bottlenecks\n\nA recurring \"war story\": students attributed slowness to CP-SAT when their model construction contained \"an unnecessarily complex O(n⁵) nested loop, which would take days to run.\" Enabling `log_search_progress` revealed the issue lay in Python code, not the solver. Enable logging to distinguish between model-building delays and solve time.\n\n## Practical Warnings\n\n- \"Callbacks can slow down the solver significantly\" by forcing frequent Python layer switches\n- \"Bad hints can still cause slowdowns by guiding the solver in the wrong direction\"\n- Presolve may prune feasible solutions that match hints; use `keep_all_feasible_solutions_in_presolve = True` if hint infeasibility emerges (at potential performance cost)"}]},"uuid":"597ab593-082d-4b48-aa3d-32112fd14df1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:39.988Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0f7d52f7-e283-4901-a50e-a4d2bf621d71","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
