{"parentUuid":"5d0f39eb-f486-44d7-9afa-e65a4a9114c4","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0113TD9RHE2UgejBaYkcGbKF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0139Xj5MfmMAkDZ3fH71oPrZ","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"or-tools\" github issue \"no progress\" hours infeasible scheduling assignment"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":746,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5052,"cache_read_input_tokens":23704,"output_tokens":311,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5052},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":746,"output_tokens":311,"cache_read_input_tokens":23704,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5052,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5052,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqppycqFBZFUFyqxjGA","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1de62a6b-b0c1-4990-8588-0073570369cb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:44.703Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fbacc061-9591-4727-ae02-fb19054bb24d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SPdkNZMANxERT9vbXTEzMf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CP-SAT\" production deployment scheduling Google Borg machine assignment hours\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Large-scale cluster management at Google with Borg\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/pubs/large-scale-cluster-management-at-google-with-borg/\"},{\"title\":\"Borg: Large-scale Cluster Management at Google with Borg\",\"url\":\"https://noneback.github.io/blog/borg/\"},{\"title\":\"awesome-distributed-systems/notes/borg.md at master · gojek/awesome-distributed-systems\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/gojek/awesome-distributed-systems/blob/master/notes/borg.md\"},{\"title\":\"Borg: A Cluster management system | by Aditya Shete | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@adityashete009/borg-large-scale-cluster-management-system-cbdcc4f8eb91\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Large-scale cluster management at Google with Borg | Random Notes\",\"url\":\"https://xzhu0027.gitbook.io/blog/cloud-computing/index/large-scale-cluster-management-at-google-with-borg\"},{\"title\":\"Large-scale cluster management at Google with Borg Abhishek Verma†\",\"url\":\"https://research.google.com/pubs/archive/43438.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Large-scale cluster management at Google with Borg | Proceedings of the Tenth European Conference on Computer Systems\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/2741948.2741964\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"Large-scale cluster management at Google with Borg\",\"url\":\"https://www.anantjain.dev/posts/borg\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about CP-SAT and Google Borg, though the results don't specifically mention production deployment scheduling with hours as a metric. Here's what I found:\n\n## CP-SAT Overview\n\nCP-SAT (Constraint Programming - Satisfiability) is Google OR-Tools' constraint programming solver that combines the expressiveness of constraint programming with the efficiency of modern SAT (Boolean Satisfiability) solvers.\n\n## Google Borg Scheduling\n\nGoogle's Borg system is a cluster manager that runs hundreds of thousands of jobs, from many thousands of different applications, across a number of clusters each with up to tens of thousands of machines.\n\nThe scheduling algorithm has two parts: Feasibility checking (where the scheduler finds a set of machines that meet the task's constraints and also have enough available resources) and Scoring, or determining \"goodness\", mostly driven by built-in criteria such as minimizing the number and priority of preempted tasks, picking machines that already have a copy of the task's packages, spreading tasks across power and failure domains, and packing quality including putting a mix of high and low priority tasks onto a single machine.\n\nThe search results do reference CP-SAT being used for scheduling applications, but I did not find specific information about production deployment scheduling performance metrics measured in hours for machine assignment. If you're looking for more specific technical details about this particular use case, you may want to check Google's research publications or OR-Tools documentation directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1b1b4e5e-feae-4e30-a925-80eddca6e2a3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:48.953Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fbacc061-9591-4727-ae02-fb19054bb24d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"abcd7501-0dfd-4bc5-bc15-eb3f4d2cbd14","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MgwFwi2RRrMSXCBV1q61VL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT lazy clause generation Benders decomposition logic-based industrial scheduling\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Planning and Scheduling by Logic-Based Benders Decomposition | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.1060.0371\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint programming and logic-based Benders decomposition for the integrated process planning and scheduling problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305048322002298\"},{\"title\":\"Enhanced logic-based Benders decomposition methods for the distributed heterogeneous non-permutation flow shop scheduling problem: International Journal of Production Research: Vol 63 , No 24 - Get Access\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00207543.2025.2553820?mi=ik0enr\"},{\"title\":\"[2601.06542] Resource-constrained Project Scheduling with Time-of-Use Energy Tariffs and Machine States: A Logic-based Benders Decomposition Approach\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.06542\"},{\"title\":\"ULD Build-Up Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_17\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-based Benders decomposition for planning and scheduling: a computational analysis | The Knowledge Engineering Review | Cambridge Core\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/knowledge-engineering-review/article/abs/logicbased-benders-decomposition-for-planning-and-scheduling-a-computational-analysis/70EE77BFAE516C56F3363A90A3786D84\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/logic-based-benders-decomposition-lbbd-4e47b3ae-690a-44a4-9d80-a191b385b4e6\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-based benders decomposition methods for the distributed flexible job shop scheduling problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221725006769\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's an overview of the key topics and their connections:\n\n## CP-SAT and Lazy Clause Generation\n\nCP-SAT uses lazy clause generation to combine constraint propagation with SAT solving. The \"lazy\" aspect means clauses are generated on-demand as conflicts are discovered, rather than pre-generating all possible conflict clauses upfront. CP-SAT provides specialized constraint types that propagate far more effectively than decomposing problems into elementary constraints.\n\n## Logic-Based Benders Decomposition (LBBD)\n\nLogic-Based Benders Decomposition is a generalization of classical Benders decomposition that integrates combinatorial, constraint-oriented subproblems for enhanced problem solving. It employs logic-based inference to generate exclusion and optimality cuts, facilitating rapid convergence even in NP-hard, nonconvex scenarios.\n\nIn LBBD, the master problem and subproblems can be solved using heterogeneous optimization technologies (e.g., MIP, CP, MILP, specialized algorithmics), with logic-based inference used for generating valid cuts.\n\n## Application to Industrial Scheduling\n\nMixed-integer linear programming (MILP) and constraint programming (CP) are combined to solve planning and scheduling problems, with tasks allocated to facilities using MILP and scheduled using CP, linked via logic-based Benders decomposition.\n\nThese methods decompose the problem into an assignment master problem and multiple scheduling subproblems, which are solved using MILP and CP. Computational experiments show that CP-based methods outperform other approaches for small-sized instances, while the enhanced LBBD methods excel for medium- and large-sized instances.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a7ac2818-3fce-4d56-a687-e6bfc7747b7d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:49.779Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"abcd7501-0dfd-4bc5-bc15-eb3f4d2cbd14","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1de62a6b-b0c1-4990-8588-0073570369cb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0139Xj5MfmMAkDZ3fH71oPrZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" github issue \"no progress\" hours infeasible scheduling assignment\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Using arcs in job scheduling with transitions · Issue #1401 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1401\"},{\"title\":\"Problem in shift Scheduling by using ortools Shift Scheduling Sat from Google · Issue #1740 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1740\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/scheduling.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/scheduling.md\"},{\"title\":\"scheduling problem with variable delays between tasks · google/or-tools · Discussion #2940\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/2940\"},{\"title\":\"Wait time constraint in job scheduling · Issue #960 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/960\"},{\"title\":\"google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1727\"},{\"title\":\"Job shop example: How the Constraints solver solve such a problem? · Issue #945 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/945\"},{\"title\":\"Combined multiple problem in Scheduling · Issue #1252 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1252\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - giangstrider/scheduling-optimization-ortools: Using Google Operation Research Tools (Ortools) to solve complex scheduling problems (General optimization problems). · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/giangstrider/scheduling-optimization-ortools\"},{\"title\":\"How to presolve the model · Issue #1463 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1463\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several relevant GitHub issues and discussions related to OR-Tools scheduling and assignment problems:\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n1. One user tested constraints for a single job to be scheduled and the solver returned an Infeasible result (Issue #1401). When they commented out the arcs constraints section it solved without issue, suggesting the arcs conflict with other constraints for low job counts.\n\n2. There are discussions about combined scheduling and assignment problems where workers are assigned to tasks and circuit constraints are used for every worker with a node for every task (Discussion #2940).\n\n3. One user encountered a problem where the solver returned 0 results when there was no solution satisfying all deadlines, and wanted the program to return the result with the least number of tasks going over their deadline (Issue #1727).\n\n4. Another issue involved shift scheduling where fixing shift requests improved solve speed, but the model could become infeasible for some inputs, and the user sought to presolve the model to handle infeasibility gracefully (Issue #1463).\n\nThe search results show that \"no progress\" and infeasibility issues in OR-Tools scheduling are common challenges, particularly with constraint conflicts, complex scheduling-assignment combinations, and deadline satisfaction problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"55b91f40-3336-4892-ad04-c0177a1f8bdb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:51.314Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1de62a6b-b0c1-4990-8588-0073570369cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5d0f39eb-f486-44d7-9afa-e65a4a9114c4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UNQKMAzAKMMLggR96tDrRW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT solver search progress stalled hours conflicts per second log analysis\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver takes way too long to shut down or does not stop at all despite given time limit · Issue #4882 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4882\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver: A big time gap between solution found and solver response · google/or-tools · Discussion #3934\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3934\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-logutils · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpsat-logutils/\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CP-SAT solver search progress, stalled progress, conflicts per second, hours, and log analysis:\n\n## Search Progress Logging\n\nThe search progress log is an essential element of the overall log, crucial for identifying performance bottlenecks. It clearly demonstrates the solver's progression over time and pinpoints where it faces significant challenges. The structure of the log entries is standardized as: EVENT NAME | TIME | BEST SOLUTION | RANGE OF THE SEARCH | COMMENT\n\n## Monitoring Conflicts\n\nYou can access internal metrics such as self.num_booleans, self.num_branches, and self.num_conflicts. These metrics are available through solution callbacks, which allow you to monitor solver progress in real-time.\n\n## Handling Stalled Progress\n\nFor cases where progress stalls or for other reasons, solution callbacks can be used to halt the solver. With these, you can decide on every new solution if the solution is good enough or if the solver should continue searching for a better one.\n\n## Log Analysis Tools\n\nThe cpsat-logutils library extracts key information from CP-SAT logs (solutions, bounds, presolve stats, subsolver activity, search progress, conflicts, etc.) and exposes them in structured Python objects you can analyze or visualize.\n\n## Additional Resources\n\nUnderstanding the log is crucial. The log is the output of the solver that shows you what the solver is doing and how it is progressing. For detailed guidance on interpreting CP-SAT logs, you can refer to the CP-SAT Primer documentation which provides in-depth analysis of log entries and their meanings.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"14c9e44b-49f8-48f7-9605-56a3b9206bf1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:51.736Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5d0f39eb-f486-44d7-9afa-e65a4a9114c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
