{"parentUuid":"42c6c74e-2d03-4fa9-99d2-45fd93c813a8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LNdAJHtTpHoX2EuojuWAW6","type":"tool_result","content":"I appreciate your interest in the CP-SAT-LP paper, but I need to be direct: the content you've provided appears to be a PDF file encoded in binary/compressed format, not readable text about a CP-SAT-LP research paper.\n\nThe material shown consists of PDF structural elements (stream objects, filter declarations, font references) rather than extractable article content. I cannot reliably identify, quote, or summarize specific claims about:\n\n- Real industrial applications and customer case studies\n- Problem sizes and runtime benchmarks\n- Available subsolvers\n- Infeasibility/optimality proving recommendations\n\n**To help you effectively, I would need:**\n\n1. A text-based version of the paper (plain text, HTML, or properly extracted PDF content)\n2. A direct link to the publication (arXiv, conference proceedings, etc.)\n3. The specific title and authors you're referencing\n\nIf you can provide the paper in a readable format, I'll be happy to extract the technical details, benchmark numbers, and application examples you're seeking—with proper quotation attribution and the 125-character limit observed.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 323.5KB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778185893204-9kjid2.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"b9e9cc54-72c9-47fb-a74a-8dedb8b2acb6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:37.842Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"42c6c74e-2d03-4fa9-99d2-45fd93c813a8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"70c877f3-a775-49c0-98dc-7602a1cecb74","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sf6q1Z3y9cDDXeQGoZyK4g","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT \"anytime\" optimization \"good enough\" production industrial accept gap suboptimal\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Optimization of Timed Petri Nets using CP-SAT - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2405896324000946\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"A practical introduction to Constraint Programming using CP-SAT and Python\",\"url\":\"https://pganalyze.com/blog/a-practical-introduction-to-constraint-programming-using-cp-sat\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CP-SAT in relation to \"anytime\" optimization and accepting suboptimal solutions in production environments:\n\n## Key Findings on \"Good Enough\" Solutions\n\nCP-SAT often finds a reasonably good solution even within a time limit, although it may not be proven optimal. This is a crucial feature for practical, production-oriented use cases.\n\n## Gap Tolerance Parameters\n\nFor accepting suboptimal solutions, CP-SAT provides explicit mechanisms: You can specify acceptable solution quality using absolute_gap_limit and relative_gap_limit, where the absolute limit stops the solver when the solution is within a specified value of the bound, and the relative limit stops the solver when the objective value is within a specified ratio of the bound.\n\n## Anytime Optimization with Callbacks\n\nWith solution callbacks, you can decide on every new solution if the solution is good enough or if the solver should continue searching for a better one. This enables true anytime behavior where the solver can be interrupted once a satisfactory solution is found.\n\n## Production Deployment Guidance\n\nFor industrial applications, the guidance includes: For production systems, implement timeout mechanisms and fallback strategies for cases where the solver cannot find a solution within acceptable time limits.\n\nAdditionally, CP-SAT can be good enough and often competitive for practical use cases, making it suitable for production environments where optimal solutions aren't always necessary.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"57d2869c-9503-42fd-a350-6e909f842d9b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:38.233Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"70c877f3-a775-49c0-98dc-7602a1cecb74","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9a850e9e-7a6d-4c4c-a788-466b88f59c5c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L8d76RAhExWGSEmVgDJzZv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" issue Perron decomposition Benders advice large problem\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ULD Build-Up Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_17\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-based Benders Decomposition for Large-scale Optimization J. N. Hooker\",\"url\":\"https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/LBBDbookChapter.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benders_decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition for Large-Scale Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-22788-3_1\"},{\"title\":\"OR in an OB World: Benders Decomposition Then and Now\",\"url\":\"https://orinanobworld.blogspot.com/2011/10/benders-decomposition-then-and-now.html\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition - JuMP-dev\",\"url\":\"https://jump.dev/JuMP.jl/stable/tutorials/algorithms/benders_decomposition/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Logic-Based Benders Decomposition for Large-Scale Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/335669137_Logic-Based_Benders_Decomposition_for_Large-Scale_Optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition for very large scale partial set covering and maximal covering location problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221718310737\"},{\"title\":\"Multi-stage Benders Decomposition for Optimizing Multicore Architectures | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-68155-7_6\"},{\"title\":\"[1910.11944] Logic-based Benders decomposition for large-scale optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.11944\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools, Perron (a key figure in OR-Tools development), Benders decomposition, and their application to large-scale optimization problems.\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**OR-Tools and Perron:**\nLaurent Perron is associated with OR-Tools CP-SAT solver version 9.6, indicating his significant role in the development of Google's optimization toolkit.\n\n**Benders Decomposition for Large Problems:**\nLogic-based Benders decomposition (LBBD) is a generalization of classical Benders decomposition that allows the subproblem to be any optimization problem, making it amenable to a wide variety of large-scale problems that decouple or otherwise simplify when certain decision variables are fixed.\n\n**Real-World Application:**\nThe search results include a practical example where large time-expanded models are produced in ULD build-up scheduling, and logic-based Benders decomposition was proposed to assign batches to time intervals and workstations in the master problem while the actual schedule is decided in a subproblem.\n\n**Effectiveness:**\nLBBD has a large and rapidly growing range of successful applications, and in many cases it leads to computational speedups of several orders of magnitude over the previous state of the art.\n\nThe search results demonstrate that Perron's OR-Tools solver can leverage Benders decomposition methods to handle large-scale optimization problems efficiently.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6834847c-3579-43e4-9322-d47ae90202e2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:39.302Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9a850e9e-7a6d-4c4c-a788-466b88f59c5c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f724497e-2cbd-4aae-b631-775e7d799165","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013Dk1L6GY1orjLnbXgrWkqB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT 2D packing rectangle placement large instance benchmark hours\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Optimal Rectangle Packing: An Absolute Placement ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1402.0557\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-primer/evaluations/packing/solver/packing_wo_rotations.py at main · d-krupke/cpsat-primer\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer/blob/main/evaluations/packing/solver/packing_wo_rotations.py\"},{\"title\":\"Implementing effective operations research solutions in OR-Tools - Superlinear\",\"url\":\"https://superlinear.eu/insights/articles/implementing-effective-operations-research-solutions-in-or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"A block-building constraint programming model for the container loading problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S030505482500139X\"},{\"title\":\"How to improve CP-SAT performance for large bin-packing problems? · Issue #1799 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1799\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Optimal Rectangle Packing: An Absolute Placement Approach\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/260039071_Optimal_Rectangle_Packing_An_Absolute_Placement_Approach\"},{\"title\":\"Table 3 from Optimal Rectangle Packing: An Absolute Placement Approach | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Optimal-Rectangle-Packing:-An-Absolute-Placement-Huang-Korf/2331ce6d040864872513b2cefc615606efb6169f/figure/5\"}]\n\nI've performed a web search for \"CP-SAT 2D packing rectangle placement large instance benchmark hours\". Here are the key findings:\n\n## CP-SAT Performance on 2D Rectangle Packing\n\nCP-SAT is good at finding a feasible packing, but incapable of proving infeasibility in most cases. In earlier versions of CP-SAT, the performance of no-overlap constraints was greatly influenced by the resolution, though this impact has evolved and remains somewhat inconsistent.\n\n## Benchmark Results and Runtime Characteristics\n\nThe search results include references to rectangle packing benchmarks with varying computational demands:\n\n- One benchmark instance with N=26 takes 3 hours, 28 minutes, and 20 seconds.\n- A branch-and-cut algorithm produces optimal solutions for the majority of 500 benchmark instances in less than 20 minutes.\n- As the scale of the problem becomes larger, it becomes more challenging to solve, but significant performance gains can be obtained by adjusting problem-specific parameters.\n\n## Parameter Optimization\n\nPerformance can be improved by adjusting problem-specific parameter settings such as use_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d, use_timetabling_in_no_overlap_2d and use_pairwise_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d.\n\nThe results show that CP-SAT's performance on large rectangle packing instances varies considerably depending on the instance characteristics and solver parameter configuration.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"88662082-5e19-4852-a668-14398a046849","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:40.053Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f724497e-2cbd-4aae-b631-775e7d799165","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
