{"parentUuid":"735b3a55-9bdd-420d-99af-e1f6888abbe7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C4Z7nJZQtYZEEUpEeUk96C","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Performance Improvement Discussion\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, I can only see the initial GitHub issue #1799 opened by lalithsuresh on December 21, 2019. The page does not contain Laurent Perron's responses or any subsequent discussion in the thread.\n\nThe issue itself presents a load balancing problem with these specific concerns:\n\n- **Search strategy problem**: \"the search starts with all tasks being assigned to the same node\"\n- **Presolve bottleneck**: \"'linear: simplified rhs' seems to be triggered a lot\"\n- **Variable reduction**: questioning whether to reduce \"numTasks * numNodes booleanVars\"\n- **Configuration question**: whether disabling model probing helps\n\nHowever, **no replies from Laurent Perron or other contributors are visible** in this webpage content. To access the actual recommendations and specific parameters suggested, you would need to visit the full GitHub issue page at github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1799 to read the complete discussion thread.\n\nThe content provided only shows the problem statement and the test code demonstrating the performance issue with 50 tasks across 1000 nodes."}]},"uuid":"864c1089-727d-4d9f-8a20-b73e33dd8c90","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:48.915Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"735b3a55-9bdd-420d-99af-e1f6888abbe7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"864c1089-727d-4d9f-8a20-b73e33dd8c90","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0193GRnums6pLWHot6sAXKY3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U6HnEwQsTbugVsFZ4T4jYC","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"CP-SAT\" \"Klotski\" OR \"puzzle\" OR \"floorplan\" hard instance solve hours days"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5067,"cache_read_input_tokens":41946,"output_tokens":521,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5067},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":521,"cache_read_input_tokens":41946,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5067,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5067,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoquGiYJy9hnZB9usvC2","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"613c9a95-1eeb-428b-8ac1-286abac3b8f6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:48.932Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5b1ff63c-027d-4018-b002-04f3cbb661f8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jf4P2xKAW3vFyhPrdNuv2t","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT \"no-overlap\" 2d \"energetic_reasoning\" \"timetabling\" packing infeasibility prove\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Parameter documentation NoOverlap2D, Cumulative · google/or-tools · Discussion #3107\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3107\"},{\"title\":\"2-SAT - Algorithms for Competitive Programming\",\"url\":\"https://cp-algorithms.com/graph/2SAT.html\"},{\"title\":\"A new search procedure for the two-dimensional orthogonal ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.dil.univ-mrs.fr/~gcolas/packing/jmma-20022015.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about these CP-SAT concepts related to 2D no-overlap constraints:\n\nCP-SAT supports parameters for energetic reasoning in no-overlap 2D constraints, timetabling in no-overlap 2D, and pairwise reasoning in no-overlap 2D. These are optimization techniques that can be enabled when working with 2D packing and scheduling problems.\n\nNo-overlap constraints for 1D and 2D can be used for geometric packing problems, scheduling problems, and other problems where overlaps between intervals need to be prevented.\n\nRegarding infeasibility detection in packing problems, energetic reasoning is a concept developed for scheduling problems that helps detect infeasibility and derive necessary conditions. CP-SAT can extract unsatisfiable cores from infeasible models by returning a minimal subset of constraints that lead to the conflict.\n\nThe parameters available include use_area_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d, use_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d, use_timetabling_in_no_overlap_2d, and max_pairs_pairwise_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d, which can be configured to enhance propagation and infeasibility detection in 2D packing problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8106733b-aa65-41c0-b0f9-45f18a87cdbf","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:54.210Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5b1ff63c-027d-4018-b002-04f3cbb661f8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"613c9a95-1eeb-428b-8ac1-286abac3b8f6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U6HnEwQsTbugVsFZ4T4jYC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CP-SAT\" \"Klotski\" OR \"puzzle\" OR \"floorplan\" hard instance solve hours days\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"I Solved Klotski - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YGLNyHd2w10\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Sam Royall — Cracking Klotski\",\"url\":\"https://www.samroyall.com/blog/post/cracking-klotski\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SAT_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Klotski Solver\",\"url\":\"https://samrroyall.github.io/klotski-solver/\"},{\"title\":\"General discussions: Klotski Puzzle - new problem - CodeAbbey\",\"url\":\"https://www.codeabbey.com/index/forum_topic/1dcc618130c007d8b2e818ad01a34dde\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - MonCaptain/klotski-solver: A program that finds the optimal solution to the classic sliding block puzzle, Klotski, by efficiently exploring the puzzle's state space.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/MonCaptain/klotski-solver\"},{\"title\":\"How to Play Klotski – Step-by-Step Guide to the Sliding Block Puzzle\",\"url\":\"https://klotski.org/en/blog/how-to-play-klotski\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about solving Klotski puzzles, though there isn't specific documentation linking CP-SAT to Klotski solving with the exact timeframes you're asking about.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**About CP-SAT:** Google's CP-SAT solver, part of OR-Tools, won gold medals at the Minizinc constraint programming competitions in editions 2018 up until 2025. The CP-SAT solver is designed for integer programming problems and is generally faster than MPSolver.\n\n**About Klotski Puzzle Solving:** The search results show that Klotski puzzles can be computationally challenging to solve optimally. One solver mentioned that for certain inputs, their solution works for about 15 minutes even on a 16GB RAM machine. Additionally, with proper algorithmic optimizations, any Klotski puzzle can be solved quite quickly, typically using breadth-first search approaches.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about CP-SAT being applied to Klotski puzzles or specific instances that take hours or days to solve. If you're looking for research papers or technical documentation on this specific topic, you may need to search academic repositories or constraint programming literature more directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b3eaa4b4-5308-45df-bc87-7b93351612de","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:54.846Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"613c9a95-1eeb-428b-8ac1-286abac3b8f6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5ac6e16a-02cd-4fe6-afec-93a5bbe816a7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011uYV9hdVHJrUqLstk7bdJX","type":"tool_result","content":"# Practitioner Experience with 2D Bin Packing in CP-SAT\n\n## Problem Specifications and Performance\n\n**Initial Attempt (Attempt 1):**\nThe practitioner tried using `AddNoOverlap2D` with `OnlyEnforceIf` indicator constraints but encountered a critical limitation. The system returned a `MODEL_INVALID` error with the message: \"Enforcement literal not supported in constraint.\" This approach proved unworkable because OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver does not support enforcement literals on the `AddNoOverlap2D` constraint.\n\n**Successful Approach (Attempt 2):**\nThe practitioner adopted an alternative strategy: transforming multiple bins into a single large rectangular area. Instead of enforcing no-overlap separately per bin, items are placed in a wide canvas of dimensions (m×W) by H, where m is the maximum number of bins, W is bin width, and H is bin height.\n\n## Real Results with Concrete Numbers\n\n**Small Dataset Performance:**\n- **Problem size:** 50 items across 6 categories\n- **Runtime:** Solved \"almost immediately\" \n- **Outcome:** Required only 2 bins despite a theoretical maximum of 10\n\n**Larger Dataset Performance:**\n- **Time limit:** 10 minutes\n- **Result:** Declared \"feasible\" but not proven optimal\n- **Assessment:** The practitioner notes this represents \"very good performance compared to MIP formulations\"\n\n## Key Technical Insights\n\nThe practitioner observed that \"replacing the one big NoOverlap2D constraint with a bunch of pairwise ones\" caused severe performance degradation, despite mathematical equivalence. This reveals solver sensitivity to problem formulation structure.\n\nThe scaling observation is practical: \"OrTools only works with integer variables and integer data. You may need to scale things so that you can work with integers.\""}]},"uuid":"8ee6bcc6-b1c3-46eb-960a-d149799aff87","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:55.590Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5ac6e16a-02cd-4fe6-afec-93a5bbe816a7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
