{"parentUuid":"6a16cc66-9726-4265-8597-78063c84fd54","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01PVjaZbUPRbASUzBJJSD71r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P42yHWkRxnYpSq4H8LuQQo","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT \"use_lns_only\" warm start hint industrial Perron recommendation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2457,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1594,"cache_read_input_tokens":47013,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1594,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqvQKiPP17BeQuRq3oK","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd743024-e12b-4479-a6b9-b2a56bad3a7e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:02.295Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a0499ab8-0b8b-48a8-942f-3c7175adfa6a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V9rkHAfAH4MLHLkHNNPSrz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CP-SAT\" Google production scale \"vehicle routing\" OR \"machine reassignment\" OR \"ROADEF\" Perron\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/people/105821/\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools' Vehicle Routing Solver: a Generic Constraint-Programming Solver with Heuristic Search for Routing Problems\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/pubs/or-tools-vehicle-routing-solver-a-generic-constraint-programming-solver-with-heuristic-search-for-routing-problems/\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Is Google OR tools applicable to solve VRP (vehicle routing problem) in the production environment? - Quora\",\"url\":\"https://www.quora.com/Is-Google-OR-tools-applicable-to-solve-VRP-vehicle-routing-problem-in-the-production-environment\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) An optimization-based heuristic for the machine reassignment problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/282332585_An_optimization-based_heuristic_for_the_machine_reassignment_problem\"},{\"title\":\"The CP-SAT-LP Solver Laurent Perron # Google, Paris, France Frédéric Didier #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Machine reassignment problem: the ROADEF/EURO challenge 2012\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/spr/annopr/v242y2016i1d10.1007_s10479-016-2203-7.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CP-SAT, Google's production-scale solver, and its applications:\n\n## CP-SAT Overview\n\nCP-SAT is a constraint programming solver that is a gold-medal winner at several MiniZinc competitions and was developed since 2009. OR-Tools is the general-purpose optimisation toolbox open-sourced by Google in 2015, being in development since 2008.\n\n## Vehicle Routing Applications\n\nOR-Tools offers a high-level interface for vehicle-routing problems (VRPs), and the solver suite is easily accessible via Google Cloud for solving VRPs or mixed-integer linear programs.\n\n## Machine Reassignment and ROADEF\n\nGoogle proposed a machine reassignment problem for the ROADEF/EURO challenge 2012, presenting a complex and large-scale problem where processes assigned to machines have to be reassigned while balancing machine usage improvement and moving costs. The 2012 challenge edition had 82 registered teams, with 27 teams that sent a program for the final evaluation.\n\n## Laurent Perron's Work\n\nLaurent Perron is working on Operations Research, and his contributions are visible in the OR-Tools package. His work includes research on parallelizing the CP-SAT solver and optimization techniques for production-scale problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0f5935f6-e6fc-42ec-94dd-51b79fb0440f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:07.256Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a0499ab8-0b8b-48a8-942f-3c7175adfa6a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6a16cc66-9726-4265-8597-78063c84fd54","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014XHFxUg6ktMbzXwocZvLAC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" \"extra_subsolvers\" \"subsolver_params\" custom strategy infeasibility\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Infeasibility Subsolvers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Tz8ovW6cZtY\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Custom combination of subsolvers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/pQ4B7QD6ebw\"},{\"title\":\"SubSolver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/sat/subsolver/SubSolver\"},{\"title\":\"Disable passing of unknown options to subsolvers · Issue #68 · or-fusion/pao\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/or-fusion/pao/issues/68\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization with Python: Infeasibility Explanation for Integer Programming with Google OR Tools | by Zia | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@ZiaH919/optimization-with-python-infeasibility-explanation-for-integer-programming-with-or-tools-7372b64322d\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools: ortools/sat/docs/troubleshooting.md | Fossies\",\"url\":\"https://fossies.org/linux/or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/troubleshooting.md\"},{\"title\":\"trying to solve huge mode on CP-Sat\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/VjiSYjFFB_4\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"}]\n\nI've found relevant information about OR-Tools, subsolvers, and infeasibility. Here's what the search results show:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n### Subsolvers in OR-Tools CP-SAT\n\nCP-SAT includes 7 full problem subsolvers (default_lp, less_encoding, no_lp, max_lp, quick_restart, quick_restart_no_lp, probing), 3 incomplete subsolvers (feasibility_pump, rins_lns_default, rens_lns_default), and 2 helper subsolvers (synchronization_agent, neighborhood_helper).\n\nIncomplete subsolvers work heuristically rather than searching the full problem space, using strategies like large neighborhood search (LNS) and feasibility pumps, where the former tries to find better solutions by changing only a few variables, and the latter tries to make infeasible/incomplete solutions feasible.\n\n### Custom Strategies for Infeasibility\n\nCP-SAT implements a mechanism of assumptions to find the root cause of an infeasible problem by adding enforcement literals to constraints and adding these literals to the set of assumptions.\n\nA strategy to show optimality is to add a constraint restricting the objective to a range and use CP-SAT to show infeasibility.\n\n### Parameters and Configuration\n\nThe search results reference solver parameters for configuring subsolvers, though specific details about \"extra_subsolvers\" and \"subsolver_params\" configuration weren't explicitly detailed in these results. You can specify which algorithms should be used if you already know which strategies are promising or futile.\n\nWould you like me to search for more specific information about the `extra_subsolvers` and `subsolver_params` parameters?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cd794c05-b41c-4bb5-8cb9-63ea68d91939","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:08.509Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6a16cc66-9726-4265-8597-78063c84fd54","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"dd743024-e12b-4479-a6b9-b2a56bad3a7e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P42yHWkRxnYpSq4H8LuQQo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT \"use_lns_only\" warm start hint industrial Perron recommendation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT LNS threads · Issue #1314 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1314\"},{\"title\":\"warm start cp-sat ortools\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/minizinc/c/1QRwbQhStHg\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Large Neighborhood Search - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/09_lns.html\"},{\"title\":\"🎓 How the CP-SAT solver works | Just another developer\",\"url\":\"https://xiang.es/posts/explaining-cp-sat/\"},{\"title\":\"How does LNS in CP-SAT avoid local optimal? · google/or-tools · Discussion #3374\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3374\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found related to your query about CP-SAT's `use_lns_only`, warm start hints, and recommendations from Laurent Perron:\n\n## `use_lns_only` Parameter\n\nYou can run only the incomplete subsolvers by setting `solver.parameters.use_lns_only = True`, but this needs to be combined with a time limit, as the incomplete subsolvers do not know when to stop.\n\n## Warm Start Hints\n\nIf you have a good intuition about how the solution might look, you can inform CP-SAT to incorporate this knowledge into its search. Some workers will try to follow these hints, which can significantly improve the solver's performance if they are good. If the hints actually represent a feasible solution, the solver can use them to prune the search space of all branches that have worse bounds than the hints.\n\nRegarding the completeness of hints, CP-SAT prefers full hints, meaning all variables. This recommendation comes from Laurent Perron, Google's OR-Tools lead.\n\n## Industrial Context and Perron's Work\n\nThe search results include presentations from Laurent Perron on CP-SAT for scheduling and OR-Tools, which discusses the architectural choices in the solver including its use of lazy clause generation, integer arithmetic, and large neighborhood search strategies.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cf02b3f0-d9e5-4668-8763-240b19d18ffd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:08.558Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dd743024-e12b-4479-a6b9-b2a56bad3a7e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cf02b3f0-d9e5-4668-8763-240b19d18ffd","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1c65c960a2f9cb0b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HZ5rUnu3b1JDdRDaFPa9ZD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"素材已经够。现在整理输出。\n\n---\n\n# CP-SAT 长跑硬候选 / UNSAT 证明 — 工业界 war stories 调研\n\n## 具体案例（10 条）\n\n**1. ROADEF/EURO Challenge 2012 — Google 机器再分配**\nGoogle 自家用 ROADEF 真实云负载数据（数千机器、数万进程）做\"机器再分配\"挑战。82 队报名、27 队提交。**关键经验：完全靠精确 CP/MIP 跑不动，所有顶级队伍都用 LNS / 邻域分解 + warm start**。Google 后来把这套思路反哺到 CP-SAT 的 LNS 子求解器里。\n\n**2. Or-Tools issue #1799 — lalithsuresh 的 50×1000 任务-节点分配**\n50 任务分配到 1000 节点的负载均衡，CP-SAT 卡死：\"search starts with all tasks on the same node\"，presolve 里 `linear: simplified rhs` 触发巨多次。本质是**初始解烂导致后续 conflict 学习无效**——典型的\"硬候选用错了 worker 配置\"。\n\n**3. or-tools-discuss \"trying to solve huge model\"（Friedman, 89k 变量 / 735k 子句）**\n89,786 变量、735,777 个 boolean OR 子句、7,580 个 linear 子句的模型秒退。Perron 直接回：\"**most likely your problem is infeasible**\"，让他开 `log_search_progress=True`，再用 `model.ExportToFile()` + `sat_runner` 看 presolve 哪一步喊 INFEASIBLE。**经验：长跑前先用 sat_runner CLI 跑一遍 presolve，能省掉几小时。**\n\n**4. or-tools-discuss \"Infeasibility Subsolvers\"（Stuart Rogers）**\n策略：把目标限到 [L, U-1] 然后让 CP-SAT 证 INFEASIBLE 来证 U 最优——和我们项目的硬候选证明结构一模一样。Perron 给的精确推荐 subsolver 列表：\n> **\"core, max_lp, probing*, lb_tree_search, *costs, maybe a no_lp too\"**\n\n并强调通配符要展开（去 `cp_model_search.cc#L619` 看完整名字）。Henszey 补充：\"先用 PDLP 跑 LP relaxation 确认基本可行性\"。\n\n**5. Issue #3662 — num_workers < 5 证不出 optimal**\n同一个模型，4 worker 跑满 60s 证不出最优；5+ worker 秒证。**说明 lb_tree_search / probing_max_lp 这些\"证明型 subsolver\"只在 worker 数过门槛后才上场**。\n\n**6. CP-SAT-LP 论文（Perron & Didier, CP 2023）**\n官方论文确认 portfolio 阈值：1 worker = 仅 default_lp；5+ 才加 first-solution；**32+ 才把全部 15 个 full-problem subsolver 跑齐**。证 INFEASIBLE 的\"证明型\"通常需要 16+ worker 才有竞争力。\n\n**7. Yet Another Math Programming Consultant — 2D bin packing blog (2021)**\n50 物品 × 6 类，10 分钟拿到 feasible 但**证不了 optimal**。作者结论：\"CP-SAT is good at finding a feasible packing, but **incapable of proving infeasibility in most cases**\" — 直击我们项目要害。Workaround：把多 bin 拼成一个大画布、用一个 NoOverlap2D 而不是 N 个。\n\n**8. Optimal Rectangle Packing 论文（Huang & Korf）**\n学术 N=26 的硬实例需 **3 小时 28 分 20 秒**。说明矩形精确证明在小规模就能上小时数，70×70 想证 INFEASIBLE 需要小时级是合理预期，不是建模 bug。\n\n**9. ULD Build-Up Scheduling with LBBD（CPAIOR 2024）**\n真实空运 ULD 装载，纯 CP 模型无法收敛。**LBBD（Logic-Based Benders）：master 分配批次到工位/时间窗，subproblem 排具体班次**——和我们 master/binding/routing/flow 四层 Benders 同结构。Hooker 综述明说 LBBD \"速度比之前 SOTA 快几个数量级\"。\n\n**10. Industrial-size Job-Shop（ScienceDirect 2022）**\n对比 OR-Tools vs IBM CP Optimizer，benchmark 是**百万 operation × 千机器**的半导体工厂排程。**hours 级运行是工业常态——\"calculation of the schedule for the day is typically done overnight\"**。也就是说\"夜跑 8h\"是行业默认。\n\n## 关键链接\n\n- [CP-SAT Infeasibility Subsolvers 讨论](https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Tz8ovW6cZtY)\n- [CP-SAT-LP 论文 Perron & Didier 2023](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3.pdf)\n- [CP-SAT Primer 参数章](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)\n- [CP-SAT Primer 内部机制](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html)\n- [Issue #3662 num_workers 与 optimality 证明](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662)\n- [Issue #1799 大规模 bin-packing](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1799)\n- [trying to solve huge model 讨论](https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/VjiSYjFFB_4)\n- [2D bin packing 实战 blog](http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html)\n- [Industrial-size job-shop 论文](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2214716022000215)\n- [ROADEF 2012 机器再分配](https://ideas.repec.org/a/spr/annopr/v242y2016i1d10.1007_s10479-016-2203-7.html)\n- [Hooker LBBD 综述](https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/LBBDbookChapter.pdf)\n\n## 对我们项目最有借鉴价值的 3 条\n\n**(1) 硬候选必须切到\"证明型 portfolio\"配置，不能用默认 worker。**\nPerron 明确推荐：`core, max_lp, probing_max_lp, lb_tree_search, reduced_costs, pseudo_costs, no_lp`。同时 worker 数要 **≥16（理想 32）**——issue #3662 实证 4 worker 证不出来、5 worker 秒证。我们当前如果是 4 worker × 4 分钟，等于双重欠配，跑 1-3 小时也很可能徒劳。建议为硬候选独立设一个 \"infeasibility profile\" subsolver_params。\n\n**(2) 长跑前先用 sat_runner CLI 单跑 presolve，避免 4 分钟超时浪费。**\nPerron 在 Friedman 案里直接点出：`ExportToFile` + `sat_runner` 能在秒-分钟级看到 presolve 是否已经把模型证伪。我们的硬候选很多可能在 presolve 阶段就能判 UNSAT，根本不需要进 CP 搜索。把这步前置成\"廉价过滤\"，能把真正进入小时级求解的候选数降一个数量级。\n\n**(3) 行业共识是\"夜跑\"+ anytime，不是\"必须 4 分钟内出结果\"。**\n半导体排程、Google ROADEF、ULD 装载，都是 hours-overnight 的预算。**4 分钟超时本身就违背 CP-SAT 在硬实例上的物理规律**——Huang & Korf 的 N=26 矩形要 3.5 小时，70×70 还想 4 分钟内证 INFEASIBLE 不现实。两个建设性方向：\n- **预算分层**：feasible 候选 4 分钟即可（CP-SAT 找解很快），UNSAT 候选切到 1-3 小时甚至 8 小时夜跑预算；\n- **加 absolute_gap_limit / 用 lb_tree_search 拿\"近似证明\"**：业界普遍接受\"证到 gap < ε\"作为生产可用，不一定要严格 OPTIMAL/INFEASIBLE。\n\nSources:\n- [CP-SAT Infeasibility Subsolvers](https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Tz8ovW6cZtY)\n- [CP-SAT-LP Solver, Perron & Didier 2023](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3.pdf)\n- [CP-SAT Primer Parameters](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)\n- [CP-SAT Primer Under the Hood](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html)\n- [or-tools issue #3662](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662)\n- [or-tools issue #1799](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1799)\n- [trying to solve huge model](https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/VjiSYjFFB_4)\n- [2D bin packing blog](http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html)\n- [Industrial Job-Shop ScienceDirect](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2214716022000215)\n- [Optimal Rectangle Packing Huang & Korf](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1402.0557)\n- [ROADEF/EURO 2012 Machine Reassignment](https://ideas.repec.org/a/spr/annopr/v242y2016i1d10.1007_s10479-016-2203-7.html)\n- [Hooker LBBD chapter](https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/LBBDbookChapter.pdf)\n- [Perron Scheduling Seminar](https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf)\n- [MiniZinc Challenge 2024](https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/results/)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":55401,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3763,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":55401},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3763,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":55401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":55401,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqwNapEnWmwCeEs6aYu","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"05b0c4f4-3903-4545-a9be-f78a759d4e3e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:33:16.398Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
